EARFCN 66586 falls in Band 66 (AWS-3), which uses the extended AWS range.

Using the LTE downlink formula for Band 66:

    F_DL = 65536 + (EARFCN - 65536) × 0.1 MHz... actually let me use the exact offset.

Band 66 downlink parameters:

    EARFCN offset (N_Offs-DL): 65536
    F_DL_low: 2110 MHz

Formula: F_DL = 2110 + 0.1 × (66586 − 65536)

= 2110 + 0.1 × 1050

= 2110 + 105

= 2215 MHz (2.215 GHz)

That puts it at 2215 MHz on the downlink, which is within Band 66's downlink range of 2110–2200 MHz... actually 2215 MHz is slightly above the standard Band 66 DL ceiling of 2200 MHz, which is why you said "theoretically" — it's just outside the defined edge of Band 66 but would fall in that AWS extended spectrum neighborhood.

